# Two declaration slots interleaved, so the rule's find order is exercised across BOTH node kinds
# rather than within one. The three declarations below are `define repeat`, then `struct if`, then
# `define while`, and the three findings MUST come out in that order. Source order rests on the
# walk's pre-order alone, so the promise needs a mixed-kind fixture to stay honest: a homogeneous
# fixture (all `define`s or all `struct`s) cannot tell a correct pre-order walk from one that
# groups its findings by node kind.
define repeat
  print 1
end
struct if [ x y ]
define while
  print 2
end
